# Causal Inference Regression Example

Small visualization and experimentation repo based on the sodium/blood-pressure example from Brady Neal's *Introduction to Causal Inference from a Machine Learning Perspective*.

The code explores how different regression adjustment choices affect prediction and estimation of the causal effect of sodium on blood pressure. In particular, it compares:

- `Y ~ S`
- `Y ~ S + A`
- `Y ~ S + A + P`

and visualizes the fitted models, estimated ATEs, the underlying causal graph, confounding through age, and the effect of conditioning on a post-treatment collider.

## Credit

The original example and data-generating setup are adapted from Brady Neal's causal inference course and accompanying code.

- **Author:** Brady Neal — [@bradyneal](https://github.com/bradyneal)
- **Original code:** [bradyneal/causal-book-code](https://github.com/bradyneal/causal-book-code)
- **Course:** [Introduction to Causal Inference](https://www.bradyneal.com/causal-inference-course)

This repository is intended as a small educational extension of the original example, mainly adding visualizations and comparisons to make regression adjustment and causal conditioning more intuitive.